From 653cffd7eeb0d4511d0049f70ae295d7d8ef7dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Itis_Sajjad <itis_sajjad@example.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: UDFPS: apply framework dim below overlay only on
 finger down

1. Keep the UDFPS dim layer transparent (alpha=0) while idle so the
   lockscreen and banking app prompts are not dimmed before touching
   the sensor.
2. Drop PRIVATE_FLAG_IS_ROUNDED_CORNERS_OVERLAY from dimLayoutParams and
   attach the dim window inside addViewRunnable right before the UDFPS
   touch overlay. Previously, PRIVATE_FLAG_IS_ROUNDED_CORNERS_OVERLAY
   placed the black dim window in the topmost RoundedCornerOverlay
   DisplayArea ABOVE UdfpsControllerOverlay and UdfpsSurfaceView, which
   dimmed the white illumination dot itself and caused optical fingerprint
   recognition to fail at low screen brightness.
3. Also reset the dim layer inside unconfigureDisplay() when an acquire
   event finishes illumination before the finger is lifted, and guard
   against division by zero in interpolateAlpha().
---
 .../systemui/biometrics/UdfpsController.java  |   8 +
 .../biometrics/UdfpsControllerOverlay.kt      |  14 +-
 .../systemui/biometrics/UdfpsHelper.kt        | 176 +++++++-----------
 3 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 110 deletions(-)

